WEBVTT

00:10.130 --> 00:11.480
Snow...

00:12.940 --> 00:14.080
Damn it.

00:14.570 --> 00:16.470
I hate the cold.

00:21.410 --> 00:22.680
What?

00:25.150 --> 00:29.620
Are you starved for someone to care for
 because the residents aren't here?

00:30.060 --> 00:31.710
What a sad hangup.

00:40.640 --> 00:42.080
Stop it.

00:42.080 --> 00:44.370
I don't heal once I get hurt.

00:44.370 --> 00:45.740
At least, not now.

01:06.310 --> 01:09.210
Is the maiden here?

01:37.070 --> 01:39.960
What have you gone and done this time?

03:12.990 --> 03:15.830
You can dive into other people's memories?

03:15.830 --> 03:18.980
I keep doing it by accident.

03:18.980 --> 03:21.640
So you weren't looking on purpose?

03:21.640 --> 03:22.440
No.

03:22.790 --> 03:27.370
But I don't think what I see is an accident.

03:28.390 --> 03:34.020
It might be something they suffered 
through or some kind of turning point.

03:37.640 --> 03:41.870
Could you go into my memories again?

03:46.700 --> 03:49.630
There are things you might not 
notice even in your own memories.

03:50.230 --> 03:51.810
I want you to check for stuff like that.

03:54.350 --> 03:58.620
But when I think about
 having to see that again...

03:59.050 --> 04:03.170
I'll help you with the language 
and math exams coming up.

04:03.170 --> 04:04.420
Huh?

04:09.130 --> 04:10.430
Here I go.

04:10.430 --> 04:11.630
Close your eyes.

04:20.740 --> 04:21.650
Stop!

04:21.650 --> 04:22.510
Why are you stopping me?!

04:22.510 --> 04:24.420
We were told to kill everyone inside!

04:24.420 --> 04:25.630
There's a child in there!

04:25.630 --> 04:26.760
The littlest!

04:26.760 --> 04:28.050
They aren't from our pack!

04:27.220 --> 04:28.270
<i>It's that scene again.</i>

04:28.050 --> 04:29.120
Still, no!

04:29.120 --> 04:31.220
I don't want to kill kids!

04:31.220 --> 04:32.150
Please, just do it.

04:32.150 --> 04:33.920
No! I can't do this!

04:34.290 --> 04:36.540
I can't kill children!

04:34.360 --> 04:35.890
<i>Werewolves.</i>

04:36.540 --> 04:39.130
And I don't want you to, either!

04:39.130 --> 04:41.910
Do you not care what 
happens to our children?!

04:42.480 --> 04:43.430
We don't have a choice!

04:44.910 --> 04:46.860
<i>She's protecting Lucy.</i>

04:55.160 --> 04:58.300
I'm sorry.

04:59.460 --> 05:05.340
May the night forever protect you.

05:11.480 --> 05:12.840
Lucy?

05:14.480 --> 05:16.410
I feel gross.

05:19.230 --> 05:22.220
So, did you find anything?

05:22.830 --> 05:24.470
I saw a child.

05:25.210 --> 05:27.130
About your age.

05:29.090 --> 05:32.410
She said she was sorry.

05:36.420 --> 05:38.220
What the hell does that mean?

05:43.720 --> 05:45.110
What the hell?!

05:46.340 --> 05:52.110
So the College remains closed 
through Christmas, I see.

05:52.350 --> 05:55.190
We haven't caught the attacker yet.

05:55.190 --> 05:56.590
I don't have a choice, do I?

05:57.580 --> 05:59.580
Just what are you trying to do?

06:02.190 --> 06:05.430
You haven't investigated
 the students, the instructors,

06:05.430 --> 06:07.510
the waste tower or the labs.

06:07.510 --> 06:10.980
All you've really done
is deploy golems to patrol.

06:11.780 --> 06:15.990
It doesn't seem to me as though you're 
honestly trying to find the attacker.

06:20.240 --> 06:24.690
Most others have more resources
 available to them than I do.

06:25.510 --> 06:31.820
I'm simply trying to accomplish
 the most I can for the least work.

06:38.820 --> 06:41.780
The College is to remain closed...

06:49.150 --> 06:55.500
When am I going to be free from this?

07:08.980 --> 07:10.460
Morning.

07:10.460 --> 07:12.910
Did you see the school announcement?

07:12.910 --> 07:15.460
We still aren't going home...

07:15.990 --> 07:19.440
Hey, it's not like we're 
getting fewer days off.

07:19.950 --> 07:23.050
The Christmas party still starts today!

07:23.660 --> 07:26.390
We'll get to eat better than usual!

07:26.880 --> 07:28.340
Damn it!

07:29.180 --> 07:30.100
There.

07:32.890 --> 07:35.370
Is this what you've been working on?

07:35.370 --> 07:36.880
Rune amulets?

07:37.480 --> 07:39.690
Thorn, huh?

07:39.690 --> 07:42.340
That's a pretty unusual rune.

07:42.760 --> 07:44.240
I just felt like...

07:45.280 --> 07:49.030
This would be the rune for me.

07:49.990 --> 07:52.350
They're for all of you.

07:52.910 --> 07:56.030
As p-presents.

07:56.690 --> 07:58.420
Oh, if you don't want—

07:58.420 --> 07:59.580
We can have them?!

07:59.580 --> 08:03.870
A mage's handmade amulet isn't
 an easy thing to come by these days.

08:03.870 --> 08:05.070
Thanks!

08:05.620 --> 08:06.910
Thanks...

08:06.910 --> 08:08.150
Where's Rian?

08:08.150 --> 08:09.890
I have one for him, too.

08:09.890 --> 08:12.880
Chasing after Philomela, as usual.

08:12.880 --> 08:14.160
Still?

08:14.160 --> 08:16.130
He still hasn't gotten to apologize.

08:18.230 --> 08:20.600
If you see him, could you give this to him?

08:20.600 --> 08:22.820
I have to go for a regular checkup.

08:22.820 --> 08:23.950
Got it.

08:24.310 --> 08:25.370
Thanks!

08:25.860 --> 08:28.200
You're coming to the Christmas party, right?

08:28.200 --> 08:29.900
You have to wear your gown.

08:29.900 --> 08:30.730
Okay.

08:44.930 --> 08:46.960
<i>Smells like Philomela.</i>

09:00.430 --> 09:01.930
Alcyone-san.

09:02.460 --> 09:03.590
Chise.

09:04.160 --> 09:05.510
Is something the matter?

09:05.760 --> 09:08.160
I smelled Philo—

09:08.690 --> 09:11.040
I sensed Philomela.

09:11.800 --> 09:13.910
I'm glad I found you, though.

09:13.910 --> 09:16.210
Is Philomela in her dorm room?

09:16.210 --> 09:17.780
I want to give her something—

09:17.780 --> 09:21.070
Lady Philomela isn't feeling well.

09:21.070 --> 09:22.860
She's unable to meet with anyone.

09:23.790 --> 09:26.780
<i>I haven't seen her outside 
of class lately, either.</i>

09:28.590 --> 09:31.690
Could you hand this to her, then?

09:32.460 --> 09:34.170
It's an amulet.

09:37.750 --> 09:38.980
An amulet...

09:40.030 --> 09:44.740
May it aid her someday.

09:51.280 --> 09:53.020
Thank you.

09:53.560 --> 09:55.710
For thinking of her.

10:24.990 --> 10:26.030
<i>Mom...</i>

10:26.630 --> 10:27.650
<i>Mom...</i>

10:28.890 --> 10:29.910
Mom...

10:30.810 --> 10:34.390
I won't do as you say anymore.

10:40.090 --> 10:46.710
I'll take you back soon, Adam.

10:52.720 --> 10:53.460
Good.

10:54.290 --> 10:59.650
It doesn't look like your curse has 
spread or been very active so far.

10:59.980 --> 11:03.600
Is the curse something that spreads?

11:03.600 --> 11:04.730
Yes.

11:05.540 --> 11:10.660
The curse you bear is very 
much like a living being.

11:10.660 --> 11:14.790
Though, it's not quite the same as the 
hexes that are practiced in sorcery.

11:15.520 --> 11:17.830
Hexes that are practiced in sorcery?

11:17.830 --> 11:21.870
Put simply, curses cast by humans.

11:22.270 --> 11:26.050
They're based on strong human emotions.

11:26.050 --> 11:30.050
Animus, regret, jealousy, envy...

11:30.830 --> 11:35.940
Such things can be used to induce 
and manipulate outcomes.

11:35.940 --> 11:39.000
Induce outcomes?

11:40.340 --> 11:43.410
Misfortune, sickness, injury...

11:43.920 --> 11:46.130
Anxiety, and even death.

11:46.910 --> 11:53.590
A basic curse might be one in which you 
tell someone that they are cursed.

11:54.220 --> 11:57.960
You know how impressionable humans can be.

11:59.020 --> 12:04.530
They might associate a random unfortunate 
event and turn it into real misfortune.

12:04.840 --> 12:09.680
In that way, you don't need even need 
to be a sorcerer to curse someone.

12:09.680 --> 12:11.530
I never knew.

12:11.900 --> 12:19.070
But curses meant to hurt another 
typically comes back to the attacker.

12:19.420 --> 12:25.670
To bring someone harm, you have to be 
ready to be harmed to the same degree.

12:27.940 --> 12:31.890
"You reap what you sow."

12:53.590 --> 12:55.970
<i>I can't remember.</i>

13:00.370 --> 13:02.290
You're unbelievably slow.

13:02.750 --> 13:05.800
Your father was nothing like you.

13:06.340 --> 13:07.720
<i>I don't know.</i>

13:08.230 --> 13:12.550
<i>I don't understand, Grandmother.</i>

13:13.750 --> 13:16.100
Why are you still alive?

13:19.980 --> 13:24.470
<i>What can I do so you'll accept me?</i>

13:27.750 --> 13:32.860
The curse you bear is akin 
to old sorcery and magic.

13:33.750 --> 13:37.170
The work of a sentient entity.

13:37.720 --> 13:42.540
It implores you to be a certain way.

13:45.330 --> 13:46.520
Which means...

13:48.620 --> 13:51.640
I'll never be free of this curse, right?

13:57.210 --> 13:58.520
Lady Philomela.

13:59.370 --> 14:00.510
I've brought water—

14:01.180 --> 14:02.550
Lady Philomela!

14:09.910 --> 14:10.990
Philomela?

14:13.650 --> 14:14.780
Philomela?

14:17.490 --> 14:18.530
Philomela?

14:21.050 --> 14:22.260
Philomela?

14:24.600 --> 14:25.400
Philomela?

14:25.400 --> 14:26.200
I can't...

14:28.360 --> 14:29.270
Philomela?

14:43.390 --> 14:45.910
I was asked to give this to you.

15:13.140 --> 15:14.720
More...

15:15.400 --> 15:18.500
I want more.

15:52.400 --> 15:53.430
Philomela?

15:54.660 --> 15:57.710
I need to gather more.

16:01.510 --> 16:02.980
Are you all right?

16:03.350 --> 16:05.000
You're well enough to get up today—

16:10.980 --> 16:15.420
I've always lived in fear of you.

16:20.610 --> 16:21.960
Still no?

16:22.260 --> 16:23.630
Show up whenever you like.

16:23.630 --> 16:27.280
I'm still not letting you in 
the girls' dorms, mister.

16:28.050 --> 16:29.240
Even now?

16:29.240 --> 16:30.850
Th-That's...

16:30.850 --> 16:32.930
Slightly good food!

16:43.880 --> 16:45.010
Chise?!

16:46.570 --> 16:47.810
Something's wrong with Chise!

16:49.680 --> 16:50.540
Chise!

16:51.370 --> 16:52.550
Ruth...

16:57.940 --> 16:59.370
What happened?

16:59.730 --> 17:00.950
It's...

17:00.950 --> 17:02.890
The magic book.

17:02.890 --> 17:06.450
It's nearby, along with the holder.

17:08.510 --> 17:09.620
What happened?!

17:25.930 --> 17:28.140
What are you?!

17:29.680 --> 17:30.600
Hold it!

17:30.600 --> 17:32.780
I'll let the teachers know!

17:45.470 --> 17:48.250
She's been corrupted.

17:52.380 --> 17:53.840
Elias...

17:54.380 --> 17:57.560
I want to help.

18:01.250 --> 18:02.500
All right.

18:04.510 --> 18:05.850
Let's chase them together.

18:08.350 --> 18:10.540
R-Really?

18:10.540 --> 18:13.400
I thought you were going to leave me here.

18:13.400 --> 18:17.910
If it's going to come after you anyway, 
we're better off sticking together.

18:20.380 --> 18:26.790
Besides, it might start sapping more 
magic out of its victims if we let it.

18:29.230 --> 18:35.210
By which I mean, I think we're both
 trying to help our friends, here.

18:38.960 --> 18:40.220
Let's go!

18:43.300 --> 18:44.210
Stop!

18:46.660 --> 18:48.700
<i>She's been robbed of magic power.</i>

18:54.290 --> 18:56.140
<i>That's the magic book's...</i>

19:04.680 --> 19:08.570
Ancient bull, sovereign 
of the land of tears...

19:09.230 --> 19:11.080
With the blood of the beginning child,

19:11.460 --> 19:14.410
let drain the red well and 
sever the root of immortality!

19:39.050 --> 19:40.520
That way.

19:41.300 --> 19:44.950
Do you still mean to consume magic power?!

19:44.950 --> 19:46.970
What's your goal?!

19:46.970 --> 19:50.170
What's worth changing into that—

19:51.900 --> 19:54.730
I can't stand it.

19:57.040 --> 19:59.810
You're always right.

20:01.010 --> 20:02.350
And strong.

20:02.760 --> 20:04.120
And honest.

20:04.540 --> 20:06.260
And decisive.

20:06.800 --> 20:15.130
Being with you, this one feels 
pathetic, and foolish, and worthless.

20:16.630 --> 20:18.410
Wait, you can't be...

20:18.770 --> 20:19.680
Rian...

20:20.940 --> 20:25.040
I've always hated you.

20:29.010 --> 20:33.490
Hey, could you get Rian to stop 
coming to the girls' dorm?

20:34.630 --> 20:37.010
Is the young master in love or something?

20:37.010 --> 20:38.920
I don't think it's like that.

20:39.580 --> 20:41.180
I think he's...

20:44.080 --> 20:45.160
Rian!

21:03.750 --> 21:05.630
Look at all of them.

21:20.120 --> 21:21.540
<i>The students...</i>

21:33.690 --> 21:35.850
I'm glad you're here.

21:36.300 --> 21:37.700
Principal.

21:39.160 --> 21:46.070
Could you please let me out of the College?

21:46.990 --> 21:48.030
Rian!

21:48.030 --> 21:49.500
Rian, are you okay?!

21:50.380 --> 21:51.340
Rian!

21:52.170 --> 21:52.910
Ow!

21:56.470 --> 21:59.430
Stop her. Please.

21:59.430 --> 22:02.290
Wait, Rian, who's <i>her</i>?!

22:02.910 --> 22:04.020
That thing...

22:08.160 --> 22:09.400
is Philomela!

22:10.290 --> 22:14.420
I must go and welcome...

22:14.870 --> 22:20.230
my mother and father, who are waiting in Hell.
